WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.042 --> 00:00:15.517
Same wrong answer, different reasons. Student A believes parallel resistors add; Student B made an arithmetic slip. Different plans.

2
00:00:15.517 --> 00:00:23.715
The diagnostic covers both chapters. Each answer collects the option, a line of reasoning, and the student's confidence.

3
00:00:23.715 --> 00:00:33.047
Our student picks 0.25 amps and explains: ‘the first bulb uses up some of the current.’ They're certain.

4
00:00:33.047 --> 00:00:48.468
The X-Ray reads the reasoning, not just the answer. It names the misconception, quotes the evidence, and gives the fix.

5
00:00:48.468 --> 00:01:02.761
Break the misconception: predict, run the experiment, see the prediction fail, explain. The tutor re-checks the explanation and closes the misconception.

6
00:01:02.761 --> 00:01:10.643
Teach it another way: the same Class 10 lesson as an analogy, an Indian real-life example, or step by step, in English, Hinglish or Hindi.

7
00:01:10.643 --> 00:01:18.086
After ten questions, the X-Ray has found four distinct misconceptions, each one backed by the student's own words.

8
00:01:18.086 --> 00:01:29.578
The concept graph shows the whole syllabus. Dashed purple rings mark root causes: weak foundations behind later mistakes.

9
00:01:29.578 --> 00:01:37.167
Explain it back: the student teaches the concept in their own words, and the tutor checks it for wrong ideas and missing key points.

10
00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:44.591
Practice targets the weakest concept, or its weaker prerequisite, at a difficulty matched to current mastery.

11
00:01:44.591 --> 00:01:52.324
The agent shows its work as tool calls: diagnose, update the learner model, find the root cause, pick and verify the next question, schedule review.

12
00:01:52.324 --> 00:01:59.828
A three-level hint ladder: nudge, trap warning, then method. Each hint lowers the mastery credit, so answers are earned.

13
00:01:59.828 --> 00:02:07.257
SM-2 spaced repetition builds a review plan. Confident mistakes come back first, and mastered concepts are spaced out.

14
00:02:07.257 --> 00:02:18.890
Proof of learning: two clean answers close a misconception as Fixed. The teacher gets a before-and-after report.

15
00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:27.534
The class agent scans 31 learner models, finds shared misconceptions, at-risk students and root gaps, and drafts a briefing for the teacher to approve.

16
00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:34.739
The teacher dashboard shows class-wide gaps: 31 students by 15 concepts, with the class average on the bottom row.

17
00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:42.170
The agent drafts the remedial lesson; the teacher approves, edits or rejects it before anything is assigned.

18
00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:50.821
On unseen wording, rules catch 28% of misconceptions; Gemini catches 94%, and 100% in Hinglish. This recording runs offline; Gemini is live at concept-xray.vercel.app.

19
00:02:50.821 --> 00:02:56.695
Concept X-Ray: fix the reason, not just the answer.
